# War Thunder Hacks SEO (all phases)

This project exists to rank for the War Thunder cheat/hack cluster. Treat SEO as architecture in every change — never a late add-on.

## Targets

- Primary: `War Thunder cheats`
- Secondary: `War Thunder hacks`, `War Thunder cheat`, `War Thunder ESP`, `War Thunder aimbot`, `War Thunder radar`, `War Thunder wallhack`
- Goal: compete for top organic positions via intent match, original content, and technical quality — not stuffing or doorway pages

## Every page / every change

- One H1; unique title and meta description; canonical via `SeoHead` / `src/data/seo.ts`
- Original copy only. Never copy competitors (including warthundercheats.org)
- Match search intent: commercial pages convert; supporting pages inform (guides, FAQ, features)
- Cover the topic in depth on dedicated URLs when we build them; do not ship thin placeholder pages
- Internal links with descriptive anchors (e.g. “War Thunder ESP”, not “click here”)
- Use planned routes from `src/data/navigation.ts`; do not invent competing slugs
- Structured data through the existing SEO helpers (WebPage, FAQPage, SoftwareApplication as relevant)
- Fast, static-first, almost no client JS; preserve Core Web Vitals
- Mobile-first, semantic HTML, accessible headings, descriptive image ALT
- Commercial CTAs only via `CtaLink.astro` / `PURCHASE_URL` in `src/data/cta.ts`
- Navigation and in-page links (`#features`, `/faq/`, feature URLs) must never point at checkout

## Content quality

- Write for someone searching the keyword: what it is, features, how it works, compatibility, FAQ, clear next step
- Use natural variants (cheat/cheats/hacks) — do not repeat the exact phrase in every sentence
- Prefer one strong page per intent over many near-duplicate pages
- Keyword ownership: `src/data/keywordOwnership.ts` and `.cursor/rules/keyword-ownership.mdc`
